@startuml
title Successful status submission — Tweeter Milestone 3
hide footbox
autonumber
participant "postStatus\n: PostStatus component" as component
participant "presenter\n: PostPresenter" as presenter
participant "listener\n: PostView (component)" as listener
participant "clientService\n: StatusService (client)" as client
participant "facade\n: ServerFacade" as facade
participant "communicator\n: ClientCommunicator" as communicator
participant "gateway\n: AWS API Gateway" as gateway
participant "postStatusLambda\n: PostStatusLambda module" as lambda
participant "serverService\n: StatusService (server)" as server
note over component,communicator: Client async methods return promises; await suspends the caller while the event loop remains available.
[-> component: submitPost(event)
component -> presenter: submitPost(post,\ncurrentUser, authToken)
presenter -> listener: setIsLoading(true)
presenter -> listener: displayInfoMessage(\n"Posting status...", 0)
presenter -> presenter: new Status(post, currentUser,\nDate.now())
presenter -> presenter: post(authToken, status)
presenter -> client: postStatus(authToken, status)
client -> client: new PostStatusRequest(\nauthToken.token, status.dto)
client -> facade: postStatus(request)
facade -> facade: performAction(request,\n"/status/post", failureMessage)
facade -> communicator: doPost(request,\n"/status/post")
communicator -> communicator: JSON.stringify(request)
communicator ->> gateway: fetch: POST /dev/status/post\nJSON {token, status}
gateway -> lambda: handler(request)\nJSON body mapped to event
lambda -> lambda: validatePostStatusRequest(request)\nvalid token shape + nonblank post
lambda -> lambda: Status.fromDto(request.status)
lambda -> server: postStatus(request.token, status)
server -> server: await new Promise(\nsetTimeout(resolve, 2000))
server --> lambda: Promise<void> completes
lambda --> gateway: new TweeterResponse(true)\n{success: true, message: null}
gateway --> communicator: HTTP 200 + JSON body\nintegration response mapping
communicator -> communicator: await response.json()\ncheck HTTP + common fields
communicator --> facade: TweeterResponse
facade -> facade: check response.success
facade --> client: Promise<void> completes
client --> presenter: await post(...) completes
presenter -> listener: setPost("")
presenter -> listener: displayInfoMessage(\n"Status posted!", 2000)
note over gateway,server: Custom non-proxy integration bridges HTTP JSON and the Lambda event/response.\nServer posting is simulated; no persistence or feed updates.
note over presenter,listener: After the displayed endpoint, finally deletes the posting toast and calls setIsLoading(false).
@enduml
